From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 23:12:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] webOS: count WhatsApp poll votes on the poll, one vote per
 voter

* Count WhatsApp poll votes on the poll itself

A vote on a WhatsApp poll came in as a message of its own under the
poll ("voted in poll ... for ..."). Keep each voter's latest choice per
poll in <username>.polls.json, the oldest polls dropped beyond 500, and
rewrite the poll message in place (webos-im-edit) with a "votes" count
for each option in its poll: token. Our own vote is counted when it is
sent, since WhatsApp does not send it back. A vote on a poll that is not
cached is still shown as before.

* Count every WhatsApp poll vote on its poll, by one voter each

A vote on a poll this plug-in had seen could still come as the line
"voted in a poll, but this plug-in failed to keep track of the poll."
The poll was looked up only in the message cache, which is written at
a clean log-out alone and holds the last 500 messages of all kinds,
votes among them: after the transport was stopped any other way, or
after enough other messages, the poll was gone.

Each poll seen (one made on our phone as much as anyone's) is now also
kept with the tally in <username>.polls.json, written at every change,
with its question, options and how many may be chosen, and forgotten
with its votes after the 500 newest polls. A vote finds its poll in the
cache or there, and is counted on it. Only a vote on a poll never seen
(from before the device was linked) is still a line, and it is from
whoever voted. A vote is no longer kept in the message cache, where it
held nothing and took the place of a message that can be quoted.

A voter is one identity in the tally: the phone-number JID without a
device. A vote from our own devices is us by our own JID, however it
was addressed, as our vote from this device is (send_poll_vote), so our
vote from the phone and from here no longer count as two voters. Anyone
else's LID is resolved through whatsmeow's LID map, or else by the
phone number the message carried beside it (SenderAlt).

The options a vote chose are matched by the SHA-256 of their names,
which is what a vote carries (whatsmeow HashPollOptions), not by the
poll's OptionHash, an optional field holding whatever the poll's sender
put there.

Our vote from this device is counted on a poll the cache no longer has,
too.

* Vote on a WhatsApp poll as whoever its key is kept under

A vote made on LuneOS was counted on LuneOS but never reached anyone.
For a poll the cache no longer has, the key is looked up by the
poll's sender, and in a group addressed by LID it is found under the
LID also when asked by the number. The vote was still made as the
number, so whatsmeow's EncryptPollVote voted as our number on a key
kept under our LID, and no one could decrypt it. Vote as the sender
the key is kept under (pollKeySender).

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [webOS specific]
